- Four loops over the input, one after another, make O(n⁴) code :: Loops in a row add up: 4n, which is O(n).
* Three nested loops over the input with `x in a_list` inside them make O(n⁴) code :: Right. The hidden pass is a fourth level: n × n × n × n.
- For big inputs, O(n³) and O(n⁴) code take about the same time :: At n = 1,000, n⁴ is 1,000 times n³. Every extra power of n multiplies the steps by n.
